anarch-bit: lets the front end cast the ray columns on several threads (RCL_CAST_RAYS_PARALLEL):
RCL_castRaysMultiHitColumns casts every step-th column from first on, each column's ray direction
computed from its index (the same values as the original running sum).

--- 12/raycastlib.h	2026-11-22 09:03:00.895583455 +0000
+++ 13/raycastlib.h	2026-11-22 09:03:00.895583455 +0000
@@ -441,6 +441,25 @@
   RCL_RayConstraints constraints);
 
 /**
+  Like RCL_castRaysMultiHit, but only casts the columns first, first + step,
+  first + 2 * step... (anarch-bit: two cores each render every other column).
+*/
+void RCL_castRaysMultiHitColumns(RCL_Camera cam, RCL_ArrayFunction arrayFunc,
+  RCL_ArrayFunction typeFunction, RCL_ColumnFunction columnFunc,
+  RCL_RayConstraints constraints, int16_t first, int16_t step);
+
+#ifdef RCL_CAST_RAYS_PARALLEL
+/**
+  Defined by the front end: casts all columns (RCL_castRaysMultiHitColumns),
+  split between threads, and returns once all are done. RCL_renderComplex uses
+  it instead of RCL_castRaysMultiHit.
+*/
+void RCL_CAST_RAYS_PARALLEL(RCL_Camera cam, RCL_ArrayFunction arrayFunc,
+  RCL_ArrayFunction typeFunction, RCL_ColumnFunction columnFunc,
+  RCL_RayConstraints constraints);
+#endif
+
+/**
   Renders given camera view, with help of provided functions. This function is
   simpler and faster than RCL_renderComplex(...) and is meant to be rendering
